  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1227 AM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nAn upper trough over the northern plains is poised to move\nsoutheast into the region today and this will drag a strong cold\nfront across the area this afternoon. With little moisture to work\nwith, this boundary will be dry with the main effect being gusty\nnorthwest winds. The main concern today will be the very dry\nconditions that persist across the area combined with the gusty\nwinds. A red flag warning is in affect for the entire area this\nafternoon. The gusty northerly winds will continue on Saturday and\nalong with min RH's in the low to mid 30 percent range a fire\nweather watch has also been issued. The dry weather will continue\nthrough the period and with min RH's in the upper 20 percent range\non Sunday and Monday, at least a limited fire weather risk will\ncontinue into next week. No rain is expected through the end of next\nweek./15/",
